                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f37b205-b56e-389d-83c6-3688d7efb582",
                        "entry_id": "0d945936-54fd-3a9d-9e99-ac490ab58718",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Athenian (an inhabitant, resident, or citizen of Athens, Greece)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0dc94fd-cab6-4786-90c1-c38e7b10da46",
                                "sense_id": "8f37b205-b56e-389d-83c6-3688d7efb582",
                                "text": "Каза́лось, под покро́вами из тума́на опеча́ленные до́чери Нере́я мета́лись и би́лись о бе́рег, опла́кивая лу́чшего из афи́нян и са́мый го́род, ослеплё́нный безу́мием.",
                                "translation": "It seemed to him that the mourning daughters of Nereus were tossing hither and thither on the shore bewailing the death of the best of the Athenians and the folly of the frenzied city.",
                                "english": "It seemed to him that the mourning daughters of Nereus were tossing hither and thither on the shore bewailing the death of the best of the Athenians and the folly of the frenzied city."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
